{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Talking About the Future"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "What Will You Do?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 14}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe situations in spoken interactions according to social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Describe situations in spoken interactions according to social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Describe situations in spoken interactions according to social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Describe situations in spoken interactions according to social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Describe situations in spoken interactions according to social contexts."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future Continuous and Future Perfect Tenses vs. Regular Future Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous tense </span> to talk about something <span class=\"underline\">happening at a particular time in the future</span>.<br/>You use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect tense </span> to talk about <span class=\"underline\">an action in the future before another action in the future</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart for a comparison of the other tenses used to talk about the future."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The Modal <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Will</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"talk about a things that are not decided; <br/>make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future; <br/>make predictions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"will + verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will remind</span> you that touching or taking anything from the reef is illegal. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Be going to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When you talk about intentions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"be going to + verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We know you <span class=\\\"strong\\\">are going to</span> enjoy a wonderful afternoon with us.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject + verb - ing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">After that we <span class=\\\"strong\\\">are serving</span> a wonderful authentic Jamaican meal.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When you talk about schedules\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject + verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The boat <span class=\\\"strong\\\">arrives</span> back at port at 6 p.m.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" the action will have started before that moment but it will not have finished at that moment\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">will</span> + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">be</span> + verb <span class=\\\"italic\\\">-ing</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will be eating</span> at 3:30 p.m. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" think of the Future Perfect tense like the Present Perfect tense, but instead of your viewpoint being in the present, it is in the future.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">will </span>+ <span class=\\\"italic\\\">have </span>+ past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">When we arrive back on board you <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will have seen</span> many wonderful creatures.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We know you are going to enjoy a wonderful afternoon with us."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Once we are there, we will hand out the fins and masks and we will give everyone a few tips about snorkeling."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We will be snorkeling at the reef for sixty minutes. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "After that we are serving a wonderful authentic Jamaican meal."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Because we will be entering a plentiful, but irreplaceable coral reef, we will remind you that touching or taking anything from the reef is illegal."}, {"type": "example", "content": "When we arrive back on board you will have seen many wonderful creatures, so we encourage you to take photos and share them."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Our underwater guides will have made sure that you have safely come up and then we will begin our meal."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We will be eating at 3:30 p.m. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "At 4:30 our band is playing and we will be encouraging people to dance. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The boat arrives back at port at 6 p.m."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le14ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "coral reef"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a hard natural structure under the sea that is formed from coral"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It will take us approximately ten minutes to reach the coral reef."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le14ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about snorkeling."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "na