ew tips about snorkeling. We will be snorkeling at the reef for sixty minutes. After that we are serving a wonderful authentic Jamaican meal.", "id": 1}, {"time": "29000", "image": "engenn9le14ob05re2img02.jpg", "text": "There are a few precautions to be taken. Life jackets are located in the bins on either side of the boat. They must be worn in the water by all snorkelers.<br/>\nBecause we will be entering a plentiful, but irreplaceable coral reef, we will remind you that touching or taking anything from the reef is illegal. We need to be respectful of this beautiful world which is home to the angelfish, clownfish, turtles and a vast array of corals, as well as other wildlife. It is advisable that you remove all jewelry, as barracudas are attracted to shiny things. So please, remove your piercings! Feeding of the marine life is strictly prohibited.", "id": 2}, {"time": "77000", "image": "engenn9le14ob05re2img03.jpg", "text": "When we arrive back on board you will have seen many wonderful creatures, so we encourage you to take photos and share them. Our underwater guides will have made sure that you have safely come up and then we will begin our meal. We will be eating at 3:30 p.m. At 4:30, our band is playing and we will be encouraging people to dance. The boat arrives back at port at 6 p.m.<br/>\nWe are happy to have you on board for this excursion.", "id": 3}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "", "text": "Welcome aboard the Cave Cruise!  My name is Captain Tom. We know you are going to enjoy a wonderful afternoon with us.<br/>It will take us approximately ten minutes to reach the coral reef. Once we are there, we will hand out the fins and masks and we will give everyone a few tips about snorkeling. We will be snorkeling at the reef for sixty minutes. After that we are serving a wonderful authentic Jamaican meal.", "id": 1}, {"time": "26500", "image": "", "text": "There are a few precautions to be taken. Life jackets are located in the bins on either side of the boat. They must be worn in the water by all snorkelers.<br/>\nBecause we will be entering a plentiful, but irreplaceable coral reef, we will remind you that touching or taking anything from the reef is illegal. We need to be respectful of this beautiful world which is home to the angelfish, clownfish, turtles and a vast array of corals, as well as other wildlife. It is advisable that you remove all jewelry, as barracudas are attracted to shiny things. So please, remove your piercings! Feeding of the marine life is strictly prohibited.", "id": 2}, {"time": "73000", "image": "", "text": "When we arrive back on board you will have seen many wonderful creatures, so we encourage you to take photos and share them. Our underwater guides will have made sure that you have safely come up and then we will begin our meal. We will be eating at 3:30 p.m. At 4:30, our band is playing and we will be encouraging people to dance. The boat arrives back at port at 6 p.m.<br/>\nWe are happy to have you on board for this excursion.", "id": 3}], "video_src": "engenn9le14ob05re2vid01"}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "video", "id": 2, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}]}]}